CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
X-WR-CALNAME:50 km ultra plan
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-23-str1-strength-strength-si@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261123T183000
DTEND:20261123T190000
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: strength (single-leg and hinge) (30 min)
DESCRIPTION:Trail and ultra running: economy\, durability on climbs and de
 scents. Lift with 2-3 reps in reserve\, stop a set if form breaks. Streng
 th starts at least 3 hours after cardio (practice).\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not
  medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-pl
 an
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24-run1-easy-run-with-stride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261124T063000
DTEND:20261124T073500
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy run with strides (65 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 42 min easy\; 6 x (0.33 min hard + 1 min easy
 )\; 5 min cool-down. Six relaxed fast strides of about 20 s (RPE 7\, smoo
 th\, not a sprint) with easy jogging between. Easy means RPE 2-3: you can
  talk in full sentences. Use your watch's easy heart-rate zone if you hav
 e one.\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you m
 ove means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-25-bike_x-easy-ride-cross-trai@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261125T063000
DTEND:20261125T073500
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy ride (cross-training) (65 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min warm-up\; 52 min easy\; 5 min cool-down. Low-impact aero
 bic work next to the running: Mostly steady endurance (RPE 2-3\, 56-75 % 
 of FTP if you use power). Eat and drink on rides over 90 minutes.\n\nWeek
  1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop
 .\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
